      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T22:28:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think so? Essentially a task that\u0027s in NMI won\u0027t get the lock and won\u0027t look at this thread\u0027s \"-\u003emm\". If we don\u0027t find any \"-\u003emm\" then we\u0027ll return NULL and we\u0027ll skip dumping this particular task. That\u0027s OK.\n\nEssentially:\n* If we return a task with a MM, the lock for that task is held.\n* If we return NULL, no lock is held and the calling function will just return.\n\nDoes that make sense?",
